## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design region-isolated pipelines, governance, and controlled rollouts with evidence of explainability, drift handling, and rollback—key for production ML in regulated environments.

## Key Concepts
- Data locality: regional storage and training
- Pipeline orchestration: Pub/Sub, Dataflow, Vertex AI
- Model governance: lineage in BigQuery, drift alerts
- Explainability: Vertex Explainable AI
- Rollback: blue/green deployment

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: Dataflow route and validate
if (record.region && isValid(record)) {
  writeToCloudStorage(record, `/region/${record.region}/data.json`);
} else {
  logError(record);
}
```
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the rollback path in a pre-prod environment?
- What would you monitor to distinguish drift from data quality issues?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests privacy-preserving ML at scale with regulatory constraints, multi-tenant isolation, and production-grade governance. Requires knowledge of Vertex AI Confidential Computing, Dataflow pipelines, Data Catalog/DLP, and automated rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Vertex AI Confidential Computing (VMs/TPUs)
- Dataflow ingestion and residency controls
- Private endpoints and per-tenant budgets
- Data Catalog governance and DLP coverage
- Adversarial robustness testing and dataset/versioning

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: basic adversarial test harness
function evalAdversarial(model, sample) {
  const adv = generateAdversarialSample(sample);
  const pred = model.predict(adv);
  return pred.accuracy;
}
```

